  "title": "LCD display module, 16 x 2 blue, HD44780 + PCF8574 I2C",
  "summary": "A blue 16 x 2 character LCD with a PCF8574 I2C backpack and a 4-pin header (GND, VCC, SDA, SCL on 2.54 mm). Wire VCC directly to 5 V and GND to ground; the backpack includes 4.7 kohm pull-ups on SDA and SCL to VCC, a 10 kohm contrast trimmer, a backlight jumper (`backlight_jumper`, default \"on\"), and address jumpers (`address`, default \"0x27\", selectable \"0x20\" to \"0x27\"). Draws about 1.5 mA for logic plus 20 mA with the backlight on. Read the two visible 16-character lines with `@<lcd>.text` (blank when the display or backlight is off, matching the blue transmissive glass) and the backlight with `@<lcd>.backlight`. Standard LiquidCrystal_I2C sketches drive it.",
